{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>When he sends you out, he will surely drive you out completely from here.</b> Rashi explained: 'all of you he will send out.' And it appears that the word כְּשַׁלְּחוֹ ('when he sends you out') is superfluous, and I say that this is its meaning: because it was evil in Moses' eyes that he was ashamed, for Pharaoh had driven him out twice — in the plague of the locusts it is written ״וַיְגָרֶשׁ אוֹתָם מֵאֵת פְּנֵי פַרְעֹה״ (Exodus 10:11), and in the plague of darkness ״וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ פַרְעֹה לֵךְ מֵעָלָי״ (Exodus 10:28). And the Holy One, blessed be He, answered him: 'Let it not be evil in your eyes, for this is an evil sign for Pharaoh — for he began with gradual expulsion, bit by bit, until the end, when all of you he will drive out. For at first it was said only \"and he drove them out from before Pharaoh,\" but it did not say that they would no longer see his face; and afterward he added to the expulsion, saying \"see my face no more\" (Exodus 10:28). But in the end, כְּשַׁלְּחוֹ — when the time comes that he sends you out — then כֻלְּכֶם יְגָרֵשׁ, all of you he will drive out, unlike the first instance, which was lighter in its expulsion, for he drove out none but Moses and Aaron; but כְּשַׁלְּחוֹ, when he sends you out — then כָּלָה גָּרֵשׁ יְגָרֵשׁ, he will drive out completely.' And this is precisely deduced from the word כְּשַׁלְּחוֹ."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:19:18.700942764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}